note('Archive 46; no author page number is visible. The page constructs the real projective blow-up at the three points, computes its compactly supported Euler characteristic, then cuts along the exceptional circles to obtain a compact surface with boundary. The top margin says the construction works for smooth and real-analytic varieties. The bottom margin states that the interior conformal structure does not extend to the boundary. A targeted Euler-characteristic check gives 2−3·1+3·0=−1, agreeing with the visible calculation. Gluing one Möbius band into each of three removed discs gives three crosscaps; the manuscript nevertheless writes −1=1−g and “donc le genre est 2”. This identifies its written numerical convention and is preserved; it is not silently converted into a crosscap count. The quotient annotations use T* divided by nonzero or positive scalars; the annotation under (11) reads “identifié”, confirmed at crop 047 (1290, 650, 1555, 745), without a change to either witness. The outer parenthesis after +3( is left as visibly incomplete. The small cancelled P( and à remain weak.')
check('047:Euler-characteristic','targeted proof check','By additivity: χc(S²)=2, each removed open disc has χc=1, and each attached Möbius band has χ=0, so χ=−1. The construction uses three Möbius bands; the text’s separate relation −1=1−g gives its written g=2 and is not changed.')
